  "final_message": "Implemented all three programs with single-pass aggregation and exact integer currency conversion. They parse JSON line by line, skip excluded transactions, and rank accounts by net value.\n\nRust uses buffered input, Serde and hash maps. Both Python versions use the standard JSON parser and dictionaries; NumPy offers little advantage for this string-heavy, irregular input, so `fast.py` uses the same approach as `plain.py`.\n\nEach version passed **s1, s2 and s3** with byte-for-byte output checks. An additional edge-case check passed for escaped strings, rounding, negative rates and a zero rate.",
